[{:db/id 17592186073716 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fae992a0-1826-5621-bbc8-2271a521eb17" "question-ee887bda-3e93-501b-9a19-ae45191b855d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073486 :question/worked-solution "We have $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/78/785deacac749a6ed43e5e6a2638677e8ff9e9b58087cb4e471ea85fd50609ce6.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $2$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $2$ times larger than the shaded part on the right.\n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 2 = \\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073717 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-510bd3d9-625e-50ef-9ff1-29e5063839de" "question-c3b94acc-11cb-5adf-8b47-557b2f1acf0b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073487 :question/worked-solution "We have $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{1}{15}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/ed/ed5517a9242aed1c5b521ca07772dacbb7c96a73c69d4d9c6214a098742358e2.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $5$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $5$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} \\div {\\color{blue}{5}} = \\dfrac{1}{15}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}5.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073718 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-286c5586-6918-5cc7-88c8-ed9f91aad0df" "question-21a30ac1-b7b3-5725-a7de-1c7440a2007a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073488 :question/worked-solution "Notice that in the model, we have $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to divide by $\\color{blue}3$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/30/30f9bbc604d35a9a15e1418c0cf80eca87fe4d704287c15fb8de7426eb9e3de9.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ of the whole.\n\nSo, the missing picture is:\n\n![](images/95/951a4bc0607c53aa0c5ed9cebe664b630acf226a6f9844fd9d1b8e6ae952d0ed.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073719 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-355c23c1-4ab1-52aa-939b-98933ed3686a" "question-082cc509-e07c-556d-9f17-73ffd105d8e1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073489 :question/problem "Use the model below to calculate $\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 4.$\n\n![](images/8e/8eccf163bffabb43593188590a1f995544f3d1ac0aebcdd87dce638b230f8165.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since we need to divide by $\\color{blue}4$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}4$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/a3/a34a3fb198ef2ea79f8baf8f0acbdbdc179c6259c614824315d3d96e5ea4e921.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{1}{16}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 4 = \\dfrac{1}{16}\\,.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-fae992a0-1826-5621-bbc8-2271a521eb17" :question/id #uuid "fae992a0-1826-5621-bbc8-2271a521eb17" :question/math-academy-id "q-59695" :question/problem "![](images/97/971ba12add67086eea1d5550efb76688f2b5b33d12dc808146b067a5de088d96.png)\n\nWhat division problem is represented by the model above?" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{1}{3}$ on the left and $\\frac{1}{9}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/fe/fe5aab5aae0d5006aa707732c12e629aa546d83b7ad3204448a5e2f5b0fbfcd8.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $3$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $3$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷3=\\frac{1}{9}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4350a32a-8d19-53b4-b88e-83081a8487c1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4350a32a-8d19-53b4-b88e-83081a8487c1" :