 :answer-field/choices ["answer-6fbfbc6b-df08-5bc6-86a1-e22399e5e9ae" "answer-b760c116-524d-5a0a-8d63-2348d6d82d9a" "answer-282af08e-d6ca-5ae5-a8a3-7b9303a4e97d" "answer-ee76ed8e-a336-52b8-9eea-6bc068665296" "answer-9df5565d-e3c2-573c-9649-b5c4eb651326"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fbfbc6b-df08-5bc6-86a1-e22399e5e9ae" :answer/id #uuid "6fbfbc6b-df08-5bc6-86a1-e22399e5e9ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b760c116-524d-5a0a-8d63-2348d6d82d9a" :answer/id #uuid "b760c116-524d-5a0a-8d63-2348d6d82d9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-282af08e-d6ca-5ae5-a8a3-7b9303a4e97d" :answer/id #uuid "282af08e-d6ca-5ae5-a8a3-7b9303a4e97d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee76ed8e-a336-52b8-9eea-6bc068665296" :answer/id #uuid "ee76ed8e-a336-52b8-9eea-6bc068665296" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9df5565d-e3c2-573c-9649-b5c4eb651326" :answer/id #uuid "9df5565d-e3c2-573c-9649-b5c4eb651326" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-082cc509-e07c-556d-9f17-73ffd105d8e1" :question/id #uuid "082cc509-e07c-556d-9f17-73ffd105d8e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-223013" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0d3157d3ef0c1514584b3f624fb1b274be37c2bd92a9c3848f4d75bebe9cb2a7.png)\n\nUse the model above to solve the following division problem.\n\n$\\frac{1}{5}÷7=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since we need to divide by $7$, we split the whole into $7$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/bb/bb8362ba449f1dc6dde21397007739a59cb9f99a240dce42970b6fd29d8d3b19.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{1}{35}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}÷7=\\frac{1}{35}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9a590395-4bd5-5e91-8534-fa05bc66616f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9a590395-4bd5-5e91-8534-fa05bc66616f" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a590395-4bd5-5e91-8534-fa05bc66616f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9639c2f8-c551-5518-8e44-6c25f7003f02" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9639c2f8-c551-5518-8e44-6c25f7003f02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9639c2f8-c551-5518-8e44-6c25f7003f02" :answer/id #uuid "9639c2f8-c551-5518-8e44-6c25f7003f02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{35}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186075052 :tutorial/content "Remember that a *unit* fraction is a fraction containing ![](images/cc/ccee5f5be0445cce59832a3def74f395a7d05cc12dc630fb36baf8f3d2d448bd.svg) in the numerator. So, for example, the fractions \n\n![](images/2e/2e38b15a8f3be74e15b87e81264b66571e593de7250dc902aeaa0e7bc1c506bf.svg)\nare both unit fractions, whereas \n\n![](images/d1/d157ce836a54214740d295f545d4c94d8c57d54d92ac7f075ed9b92556c932b1.svg)\nare *not* unit fractions.\n\nIn this lesson, we will use models to divide unit fractions by whole numbers. \n\nLet's use a fraction model to find the value of \n\n![](images/d8/d8815c6716e962ce4aebee24d004d4c591a1bc35c5fdebcd87d26ace61ead7fb.svg)\nWe start with a square model of ![](images/9f/9fcebe90d169f37bbdbf55f9e4ac86ceaf6ea6d573d101f382a12008bb0c5c2a.svg) split *vertically*.\n\n![](images/cc/ccfe0f457342c456200c98cfc46e63bdc1153698282085164eeafae5c2092c45.png)\n\nTo divide ![](images/9a/9ae11798da63cafee6ce5ccf824a7b96f9f7407a4ee445d1431d907c36f5dd1b.svg) by ![](images/db/dbfe30ca4e672459c180bd90f25f84f025162b8ce73260773fb1fbdf39b0a052.svg) we split the above whole into ![](images/6f/6f33d8df0d08ae9bddce540bedf62f46e93e748e4a5b6fd85b1dc626953e44a6.svg) equal parts *horizontally*. Then, we remove any shaded parts that are not in the bottom row.\n\n![](images/79/7940073ba05d3136ee1d465530a60bc3624b7aa06fd7484d30797758a28976d7.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents ![](images/42/42accbcb8cbfd14800ac4a27bc87d5ba529ff4173a91499f32705cd41b0c88b0.svg) of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n![](images/f1/f14a0f0f9efb98bdfe6cf40f4b1bbb2c88dc20272caaf9d604fcc44bce79d53c.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073948 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
